Package: hd-base
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3, sudo, kbd, hd-network,
 openssh-server, kitty-terminfo, ufw,
 zfs-dkms, zfsutils-linux, zfs-initramfs, build-essential, initramfs-tools,
 firmware-linux, firmware-qlogic, efibootmgr,
 locales, keyboard-configuration, console-setup, ca-certificates,
 systemd-resolved,
 eza, fzf, nfs-common, psmisc, net-tools, pciutils, usbutils, acpi,
 bash-completion, git, git-delta, ack, command-not-found, man-db, apt-file,
 systemd-zram-generator
Conflicts: zram-tools
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian base system
 Depends on the packages that every hyprdebian system has, so that they are
 installed with it and stay installed: the network configuration of
 hd-network, the SSH server and the firewall, ZFS with the tools to build its
 module, the firmware, the console, name resolution, and the
 command line tools.
 .
 It also installs hd-up, which upgrades the system after a ZFS snapshot,
 hd-reboot and hd-poweroff, which work on a desktop and without one,
 and the files that new users get in their home directory: aliases for eza
 and fzf, a git config with delta, and a nano config. It adds ~/.local/bin to
 the PATH, keeps ifupdown, os-prober and turnstile from being installed, and
 turns Num Lock on at the console login. It sets up the zram swap, the
 resolver without a stub, masks the units HyprDebian does not use, and
 points /etc/resolv.conf at the name servers of systemd-resolved.
 After a login it shows the HyprDebian banner and the state of the system:
 the pools, the RAID arrays and the failed units. Above the login prompt it
 shows the version, the type of the installation and the suite, written in
 /etc/issue by hd-issue.
